            <ArticleTitle>Tuning the dual emissions of a monoruthenium complex with a dangling coordination site by solvents, O2, and metal ions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>292-297</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7dt04198e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A polypyridyl monoruthenium complex with a dangling coordination site shows dual fluorescence/phosphorescence emissions at room temperature. The emission properties can be modulated by multiple stimuli including solvents, O2, and metal ions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
